    "_and_the_admissible_class_is_not_monotone_in_n": "k = n - 1 gives a tie floor of exactly 1/n, so 'all but one head tied' clears alpha = 0.05 from n = 20 upward and fails below it. The column therefore jumps 17 -> 19 between 19 and 20 survivors. That is arithmetic and not a glitch, and it is why the table is reported as a table rather than as a rule of thumb: the constraint is on the largest class, and 'a big share of them may be tied' is true at one n and false at the n below it.",
